  "generated_text": "To determine what percent of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is shaded, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the dimensions of the rectangle:**\n   Let the width of the rectangle be \\( w \\). Since the rectangle is four times as long as it is wide, the length of the rectangle is \\( 4w \\).\n\n2. **Identify the coordinates of the points:**\n   - \\( A = (0, 1) \\)\n   - \\( B = (0, 0) \\)\n   - \\( C = (4w, 0) \\)\n   - \\( D = (4w, 1) \\)\n   - \\( E \\) is the midpoint of \\( \\overline{BC} \\), so \\( E = (2w, 0) \\)\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the rectangle:**\n   The area \\( A_{\\text{rectangle}} \\) of the rectangle is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{rectangle}} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} = 4w \\times w = 4w^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the area of the shaded regions:**\n   - The shaded region on the left side of the rectangle is a right triangle with vertices \\( A \\), \\( E \\), and \\( D \\).\n     - The base of the triangle is \\( w \\) (from \\( A \\) to \\( E \\)).\n     - The height of the triangle is \\( w \\) (from \\( A \\) to \\( D \\)).\n     - The area of this triangle is:\n       \\[\n       A_{\\text{left triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times w \\times w = \\frac{1}{2} w^2\n       \\]\n\n   - The shaded region on the right side of the rectangle is a right triangle with vertices \\( B \\), \\( E \\), and \\( C \\).\n     - The base of the triangle is \\( 2w \\) (from \\( B \\) to \\( E \\)).\n     - The height of the triangle is \\( w \\) (from \\( B \\) to \\( C \\)).\n     - The area of this triangle is:\n       \\[\n       A_{\\text{right triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2w \\times w = w^2\n       \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total shaded area:**\n   The total shaded area \\( A_{\\text{shaded}} \\) is the sum of the areas of the two triangles:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{shaded}} = A_{\\text{left triangle}} + A_{\\text{right triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} w^2 + w^2 = \\frac{1}{2} w^2 + \\frac{2}{2} w^2 = \\frac{3}{2} w^2\n   \\]\n\n6. **Determine the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded:**\n   The percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage shaded} = \\left( \\frac{A_{\\text{shaded}}}{A_{\\text{rectangle}}} \\right) \\times 100\\%\n   \\]\n   Substituting the areas we found:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage shaded} = \\left( \\frac{\\frac{3}{2} w^2}{4w^2} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{3}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{3}{8} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 37.5\\%\n   \\]\n\nThus, the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is \\(\\boxed{37.5}\\).",
